  "notes": "West leads the ♦9 against 6NT. If West wins the ♦A and returns the suit South will make the contract despite the fact that both spades and hearts are not breaking as long as one defender has length in both suits.\n\nOn the last round of clubs, West, holding length in both spades and hearts, will be squeezed. A spade discard will establish a trick for South's fourth spade. A heart discard will allow North's hearts to run.\n\nEast can make South's task more difficult by ducking the ♦A at trick 1. East has essentially refused to rectify South's loser count down to 1. A simple squeeze can no longer function. A 2 loser squeeze, known as a stepping stone squeeze, can be executed to make the contract.\n\nTo clarify the position (although this is not necessary), South can cash 2 rounds of hearts and 3 rounds of spades. On the last club, West must keep both of his hearts and a spade guard. West is thus forced to part with his low diamond, his link to East's ♦A.\n\nSouth can now cash his remaining heart honour and exit a spade. West wins the spade trick, but he must lead a heart to North's ♥A at trick 13. The stepping stone squeeze is a 2 loser, 3 suit squeeze that can be used to enable declarer to take tricks that would normally not be available due to a blocked suit.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♦9 against 6NT. If West wins the ♦A and returns the suit South will make the contract despite the fact that both spades and hearts are not breaking as long as one defender has length in both suits.",
    "On the last round of clubs, West, holding length in both spades and hearts, will be squeezed. A spade discard will establish a trick for South's fourth spade. A heart discard will allow North's hearts to run.",
    "East can make South's task more difficult by ducking the ♦A at trick 1. East has essentially refused to rectify South's loser count down to 1. A simple squeeze can no longer function. A 2 loser squeeze, known as a stepping stone squeeze, can be executed to make the contract.",
    "To clarify the position (although this is not necessary), South can cash 2 rounds of hearts and 3 rounds of spades. On the last club, West must keep both of his hearts and a spade guard. West is thus forced to part with his low diamond, his link to East's ♦A.",
    "South can now cash his remaining heart honour and exit a spade. West wins the spade trick, but he must lead a heart to North's ♥A at trick 13. The stepping stone squeeze is a 2 loser, 3 suit squeeze that can be used to enable declarer to take tricks that would normally not be available due to a blocked suit."
  ],
